<Project>

  <!--
    CREST Phase Z (extended): override the BUTRModule SDK's destructive
    auto-deploy targets with no-op stubs. The SDK's Basic.targets defines
    CopyBinariesWindows (which wipes Modules/CREST/bin with Clean=true and
    repopulates from the current csproj's TargetDir) and CopyModule (which
    overwrites Modules/CREST/SubModule.xml from this repo's _Module/
    template). All 5 Crest.* repos share ModuleId=CREST so they take turns
    clobbering each other's deploys; whichever builds last wins.

    Phase Z's <DisableModuleCopy>true</DisableModuleCopy> only skipped the
    SDK's PostBuildCopyToModules orchestrator. The two child targets are
    each independently bound via AfterTargets="PostBuildEvent" and have no
    DisableModuleCopy gate, so they fire anyway.

    The fix: redeclare both targets here. MSBuild's "last target definition
    wins" rule means our empty targets replace the SDK's. Directory.Build.targets
    in src/ imports ../build/*.targets, which gets evaluated AFTER the SDK
    NuGet's Basic.targets, so we win.

    Manual deploy is handled by phase-w*.ps1's Verify-Copy step (additive,
    no Clean=true), and SubModule.xml is canonical-restored by phase-z*.ps1.
  -->

  <Target Name="CopyBinariesWindows" />
  <Target Name="CopyModule" />

</Project>
